# <Migrating from vX to vY>

<Punchline: Upgrade your services from v1 to v2 with zero runtime downtime in under 15 minutes by replacing deprecated configuration keys and updating client initialization.>

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Breaking Changes Summary**:
> - Replaced legacy `auth_token` parameter with Bearer token header in `ClientConfig`.
> - Deprecated REST endpoint `/v1/events` in favor of streaming WebSocket pipeline.
> - Bumped minimum runtime requirement to Node 20 LTS or Python 3.11+.

---

## Upgrade Readiness Checklist

- [ ] Verify test suite passes on existing version (`npm test` or `pytest`).
- [ ] Ensure all deprecated API usage warnings are resolved.
- [ ] Audit dependencies for ecosystem compatibility.

---

## Step-by-Step Migration

### Step 1 — Bump Package Dependencies

Update your package manifest to the latest release:

```bash
# Node.js
npm install @org/sdk@^2.0.0

# Python
pip install --upgrade "org-sdk>=2.0.0,<3.0.0"
```

---

### Step 2 — Code Transformations (Before / After)

Replace deprecated initialization signatures with the unified configuration object.

#### Client Initialization

**Legacy (v1):**
```typescript
// Deprecated v1 pattern
import { Client } from '@org/sdk';

const client = new Client('my-api-key', 'https://api.v1.org');
await client.connect();
```

**Modern (v2):**
```typescript
// Modern v2 pattern
import { createClient } from '@org/sdk';

const client = createClient({
  apiKey: process.env.ORG_API_KEY,
  endpoint: 'https://api.v2.org',
  retryPolicy: { maxRetries: 3, backoffMs: 250 },
});
await client.connect();
```

---

### Step 3 — Configuration Key Mapping

| Legacy Key (v1) | Replacement Key (v2) | Type | Migration Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `auth_token` | `credentials.apiKey` | String | Now read from structured credentials block |
| `timeout_sec` | `timeoutMs` | Integer | Converted from seconds to milliseconds |
| `use_ssl` | `tls.enabled` | Boolean | Defaults to `true` |

---

## Verification & Rollback

### Automated Verification Command
Run the integration test suite targeting the migration changes:

```bash
npm run test:e2e -- --grep="v2-upgrade"
```

```
✓ 12 integration tests passing (420ms)
```

### Rollback Plan
If unexpected runtime regressions emerge, revert the package pin:

```bash
npm install @org/sdk@1.9.4 --save-exact
git checkout HEAD~1 package.json package-lock.json
```
